WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:08.993
1945: Igor Gouzenko defected from the Soviet embassy in Ottawa, exposing a GRU spy ring that had penetrated the Canadian government.

00:00:08.943 --> 00:00:11.227
Eighteen people were convicted.

00:00:11.227 --> 00:00:18.829
1957 through the 1970s: Operation FEATHERBED investigated Soviet penetration of Canadian institutions.

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:24.238
The Mitrokhin Archive later confirmed Soviet-controlled assets had operated within Canada.

00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:28.022
1970: the FLQ October Crisis.

00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:31.534
Four hundred and ninety-seven arrested, none convicted.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:35.215
Cuba-backed separatism exploited by the War Measures Act.

00:00:35.215 --> 00:00:42.488
Jeffrey Delisle — a Navy officer — sold Five Eyes intelligence to the GRU for seven years before the FBI tipped Canada.

00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:49.784
The Airbus-Schreiber affair: Prime Minister Mulroney received over two hundred and twenty-five thousand dollars in cash payments.

00:00:49.784 --> 00:00:58.545
The Somalia affair: the Airborne Regiment tortured a Somali teenager, and the Department of National Defence covered it up until Chrétien shut down the inquiry.

00:00:58.545 --> 00:01:02.784
The Sponsorship Scandal: one hundred million dollars in kickbacks.

00:01:02.784 --> 00:01:06.772
The Liberal Party was ordered to repay one point one four million.

00:01:06.772 --> 00:01:15.681
In 2024, the NSICOP report found sitting Members of Parliament acting as witting participants in foreign intelligence operations — and classified their names.

00:01:15.681 --> 00:01:18.556
Eighty-one years of documented subversion.

00:01:18.556 --> 00:01:20.999
The trajectory is not a theory.

00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:22.852
It is a timeline.
